-- ============================================================================
-- 0009 — backfill photos onto the pre-existing catalogue, and promote two rows
--
-- Part 1: photo_refs for 28 of the 54 original hotspots
--
--   The 2026 research found Google Places photos for places the original seed
--   already covered. Attaching them is purely additive: `images` is untouched,
--   and `resolvePhotos` in src/lib/data/photos.ts puts self-hosted files first,
--   so the curated photography still leads and these become gallery extras.
--
--   This matters more than "more pictures". Part of public/file-uploads is
--   known to be wrong — Dutch maps and generic resort stock filed under Manipur
--   subjects. These references are tied to a named place on Google and give
--   every one of these rows a verified fallback.
--
--   Each update is guarded by `jsonb_array_length(photo_refs) = 0`, so it will
--   not overwrite refs added later and is safe to re-run.
--
-- Part 2: two slugs that 0008 skipped
--
--   `kachouphung-lake` and `zeilad-lake` already existed, so ON CONFLICT DO
--   NOTHING left them at weight 0 and they sorted with the old cohort despite
--   being part of the 2026 pass. Promoted here. Their existing descriptions and
--   images are deliberately left alone — the original editorial is better than
--   what the research file carries for them.
-- ============================================================================

begin;

